# VitalQ hw_v1 schematic

The electrical source of truth is `hardware/pcb/vitalq_hw_v1.py` and the
`@subcircuit` modules next to it (`power`, `usb`, `mcu`, `spi_afes`,
`i2c_sensors`, `contact`). Do not hand-edit generated files:
`vitalq_hw_v1.net`, `vitalq_hw_v1.kicad_sch`, the other `*.kicad_sch` sheets,
`vitalq_hw_v1.kicad_pcb`, `vitalq_hw_v1_bom.csv`, or `vitalq_hw_v1.pdf`.

Regenerate with `hardware/pcb/check.sh`. That script needs KiCad 9 (`kicad-cli`,
`pcbnew`) and SKiDL 2.3 in a virtualenv. It runs SKiDL `ERC()` and
`kicad-cli sch erc`. Both must report zero errors.

The schematic is hierarchical sheets of global labels and power symbols.
`vitalq_hw_v1.py` sets `net.stub = True` on every net before
`generate_schematic` because the SKiDL wire router does not finish on this
netlist. Leave `auto_stub=False`. Turning it on runs a two-pin snap pass
that stacks passives and shorts nets in the schematic. Do not turn stubs
off to "draw the wires" unless the router is known to exit.

Local symbols and footprints live in `hardware/pcb/lib/` and are produced by
`hardware/pcb/lib/make_libs.py`. Datasheet pages are in `hardware/pcb/lib/SOURCES.md`.
Use a stock KiCad symbol only after its pin numbers and footprint have been
checked. The stock `XC6206PxxxMR` symbol has the Torex pinout swapped; use the
local `XC6206` symbol.

Wiring rules that are easy to break:

- ESP32-WROOM-32E-N8R2. GPIO16 is PSRAM. Leave symbol pin 27 and GPIO6–11
  unconnected. GPIO12 stays open (MTDI low). GPIO2 stays open. GPIO15 is
  CS_AD5940 and must stay pulled up.
- Analog sense uses ADC1 only: GPIO36 (FSR) and GPIO39 (battery). Do not move
  those nets onto GPIO0–GPIO26 or GPIO32–33 if Wi-Fi is in use; those include
  ADC2.
- 3V3_D (`+3V3`, AP2112) is the ESP32 rail. 3V3_A (`+3.3VA`, TPS7A2033) is
  AD5940, ADS1292R, and AFE4900 RX/IO. 3V3_S is the I2C rail. 1V8 is AS7341.
  CP2102N VDD is its own regulator output and is not tied to 3V3_D.
- AFE4900 TX_SUP comes from VSYS. There is no boost.
- `PWR_FLAG` parts are schematic-only. `vitalq_hw_v1.py` strips them from the
  netlist. Do not give them a footprint.
- The board file places footprints on an import grid so the ratsnest is
  visible. Do not treat those coordinates as a layout, and do not route the
  board from this workflow.

This board is a research prototype. Do not describe it as a medical device or
claim safety, sterility, or regulatory compliance. Electrode resistors and
capacitors are application networks, not patient protection.
